-- title:
--   Diagonal identity β̄^*ᾱ_* = Uₚ + σ_* for p ∤ N
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, and let $N$ and $p$ be nonzero natural numbers with $p$ prime and $p \nmid N$. The assertion is that the predicate `HeckeDiagonalIdentity L N p` holds, i.e. that the following identity of divisors is valid under the hypotheses it carries: assuming that the $L$-subfields `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull (N*p))` and `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull (N*p*p))` of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ — the $L$-subfields generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfields generated by the divisor expansions of the indicated levels — both satisfy `HasPrincipalDivisors`, that is, every nonzero element $f$ has a finitely supported divisor taking the value $\mathrm{ord}_v f$ at each place $v$ and of degree $0$; given integrality of the ring maps underlying `heckeAlphaBar L N p` (the inclusion of the level-$N$ field into the level-$Np$ field) and `heckeBetaBar L N p` (the map induced by $q \mapsto q^{p}$ on Laurent expansions), and likewise of `heckeAlphaBar L (N*p) p` and `heckeBetaBar L (N*p) p`; given an $L$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of the level-$Np$ field such that `heckeBetaBar L N p` followed by $\sigma$ equals `heckeAlphaBar L N p`, with $\sigma$ integral as a ring map; then for every divisor $D$ on the level-$Np$ field (a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on its places), the pullback along `heckeBetaBar L N p` of the pushforward along `heckeAlphaBar L N p` of $D$ equals `heckeDivBar` at level $Np$ and prime $p$ — the divisor correspondence attached to the pair (`heckeBetaBar L (N*p) p`, `heckeAlphaBar L (N*p) p`) — applied to $D$, plus the pushforward of $D$ along $\sigma$.
--
--   This is the divisorial form of the Mackey decomposition of the double coset $\Gamma_0(Np)\backslash\Gamma_0(N)/\Gamma_0(Np)$ for $p \nmid N$: the self-composite $\bar\beta^*\bar\alpha_*$ of the two degeneracy maps between levels $N$ and $Np$ splits as the Hecke correspondence $U_p$ at level $Np$ plus the pushforward along the Atkin–Lehner automorphism at $p$, which here appears as the hypothesised automorphism $\sigma$ intertwining the two degeneracy maps. It is used by [`ModularCurve.degeneracyPushforwardPair_zero_heckeOperatorBar_self`](thm.html#ModularCurve.degeneracyPushforwardPair_zero_heckeOperatorBar_self).
